    "body": "[P2] This pin breaks CacheBlend on current vLLM. With blending enabled for Llama/Qwen, LMCache 0.4.4 loads `lmcache.v1.compute.attention.flash_attn`, which imports `from vllm.attention import Attention`. That module no longer exists, so initialization raises `ModuleNotFoundError`. LMCache 0.5.5 has a fallback to `vllm.model_executor.layers.attention.attention`; 0.4.4 does not. Could we use a CUDA 12-compatible version with that fix, or backport it, and add a blending smoke test? I verified the missing import against the published 0.4.4 wheel and this PR head; the passing image builds do not exercise this runtime path.",
